-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 34: ARBITRAL PROCEEDINGS (lines 5051 to 5211 of the source).  LAYER 1: the law, objectively.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  Every decision function answers `MAYBE BOOLEAN` unless it says otherwise.
--   JUST TRUE    the Order says yes on these facts.
--   JUST FALSE   the Order says no in its own words: a "provided that", an "if" or "where" that is not met,
--                a period that has run, a flat negative.
--   NOTHING      the Order does not answer on these facts: a bare "must" that has not been met (the text
--                does not say what follows; O 3 r 2(4), outside this range, lists what the Court may do on
--                non-compliance), a scope limit, a power or a term outside the sources.
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- O 3 r 2(1) is a caveat on every answer: the requirements are subject to the Court's discretion to order otherwise.
--
-- PERIODS.  The count of a period (when it begins, non-court days, the last day) is O 3 r 3, in another part.
-- Every "in time" function takes `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` as a DATE, and a filing or service
-- date as a plain DATE.  A period the text fixes in its own words answers JUST FALSE outside it.
--
-- SEAMS.  Order 19 Rule 10 (r 6(11), r 7(7)(j)), Order 8 Rules 2, 3, 7 and 8 (r 10(3), r 14(3)) and Order 15
-- Rule 4 (r 12) are other parts'.  Each is asked as "does it apply", not restated.

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 34 -- arbitral proceedings`
-- ===========================================================================

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 1 -- definitions of this Order`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:5054 | 1. In this Order — “Act” means the Arbitration Act, and any reference to a section is, unless it is otherwise expressly provided, a reference to a section in the Act;
@ref O 34 r 1 “Act” (src:5054-5054)
GIVEN `the instrument is the Arbitration Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 34 r 1 the Act is the Arbitration Act` MEANS
    IF `the instrument is the Arbitration Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“Act” means the Arbitration Act"

-- src:5054 | 1. In this Order — “Act” means the Arbitration Act, and any reference to a section is, unless it is otherwise expressly provided, a reference to a section in the Act;
@ref O 34 r 1 a reference to a section (src:5054-5054)
GIVEN `it is otherwise expressly provided that the reference is to something else` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 34 r 1 a reference to a section is a reference to a section in the Act` MEANS
    IF `it is otherwise expressly provided that the reference is to something else`
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless it is otherwise expressly provided"
    ELSE JUST TRUE

-- src:5055 | “appellate court” has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Act;
@ref O 34 r 1 “appellate court” (src:5055-5055)
GIVEN `arbitration act s 2(1) the court is an appellate court` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 34 r 1 appellate court has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `arbitration act s 2(1) the court is an appellate court`
    WHEN JUST answer THEN JUST answer
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Act", and the Arbitration Act is not among the sources

-- src:5056 | “arbitral tribunal” has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Act.
@ref O 34 r 1 “arbitral tribunal” (src:5056-5056)
