GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 34 r 1 arbitral tribunal has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Act` MEANS
    CONSIDER `arbitration act s 2(1) the body is an arbitral tribunal`
    WHEN JUST answer THEN JUST answer
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the Act", and the Arbitration Act is not among the sources

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 2 -- matters for a Judge in person`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The applications that rules 2 and 3 name, one constructor for each paragraph.  `o 34 r 2 other application`
-- is how an application these rules do not name is asked about.
DECLARE `o 34 r 2 kind of application` IS ONE OF
    `o 34 r 2(1)(a) application to challenge an arbitrator under section 15(4)`
    `o 34 r 2(1)(b) application to remove an arbitrator under section 16`
    `o 34 r 2(1)(c) application to decide on the arbitral tribunal's ruling on jurisdiction under section 21(9)`
    `o 34 r 2(1)(d) application to determine a question of law under section 45`
    `o 34 r 2(1)(e) application to set aside an award under section 48`
    `o 34 r 2(1)(f) application for permission to appeal under section 49(3)(b)`
    `o 34 r 2(2) appeal on a question of law under section 49(3)(a)`
    `o 34 r 3(1)(a) application to reinstate discontinued proceedings under section 6(4)`
    `o 34 r 3(1)(b) application for permission to enforce interim orders or directions of an arbitral tribunal under section 28(4)`
    `o 34 r 3(1)(c) application for an order in support of arbitral proceedings under section 31`
    `o 34 r 3(1)(d) application for an extension of time under section 10 or 36`
    `o 34 r 3(1)(e) application for an order under section 41(2) where the arbitral tribunal withholds its award for non-payment of fees and expenses`
    `o 34 r 3(1)(f) application for permission to enforce an award under section 37 or 46`
    `o 34 r 3(1)(g) application to hear an application in open court under section 56`
    `o 34 r 3(1)(h) application for directions on publishing information relating to an application heard in private under section 57`
    `o 34 r 2 other application`

-- Paragraph (1) lists (a) to (f).
GIVEN kind IS A `o 34 r 2 kind of application`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`o 34 r 2(1) the kind is one of paragraphs (a) to (f)` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `o 34 r 2(1)(a) application to challenge an arbitrator under section 15(4)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `o 34 r 2(1)(b) application to remove an arbitrator under section 16` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `o 34 r 2(1)(c) application to decide on the arbitral tribunal's ruling on jurisdiction under section 21(9)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `o 34 r 2(1)(d) application to determine a question of law under section 45` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `o 34 r 2(1)(e) application to set aside an award under section 48` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `o 34 r 2(1)(f) application for permission to appeal under section 49(3)(b)` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- src:5058 | 2. —(1) Every application to a Judge — ( a )
-- src:5059 | to challenge an arbitrator under section 15(4);
