      `the application is made to a Judge` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 34 r 2(1) the application must be made by originating application` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the application is made to a Judge` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Every application to a Judge"
        IF `o 34 r 2(1) the kind is one of paragraphs (a) to (f)` kind THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the paragraph names applications (a) to (f) and is silent on the rest

-- src:5071 | (2) An appeal with the agreement of all the other parties to the arbitral proceedings under section 49(3)( a ) must be made by originating application.
@ref O 34 r 2(2) (src:5071-5071)
GIVEN kind IS A `o 34 r 2 kind of application`
      `all the other parties to the arbitral proceedings agree to the appeal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 34 r 2(2) the appeal must be made by originating application` MEANS
    IF kind EQUALS `o 34 r 2(2) appeal on a question of law under section 49(3)(a)` AND `all the other parties to the arbitral proceedings agree to the appeal`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An appeal with the agreement of all the other parties to the arbitral proceedings under section 49(3)( a )"

