-- The text names the way for each case: a summons without notice where an action is pending (paragraph (2)),
-- an originating application without notice in any other case.  "On such terms as the Court thinks fit" is
-- the Court's own discretion: no function here fixes the terms.
-- src:5091 | (3) Where the case is one of urgency or an application under section 37 or 46 for permission to enforce an award, such application may be made by summons without notice or by originating application without notice (as the case may be) on such terms as the Court thinks fit.
@ref O 34 r 3(3) (src:5091-5091)
GIVEN kind IS A `o 34 r 2 kind of application`
      `the case is one of urgency` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an action is pending` IS A BOOLEAN
      way IS A `o 34 r 2 way an application is made`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 34 r 3(3) the application without notice is made in the way this paragraph names` MEANS
    CONSIDER `o 34 r 3(3) this paragraph permits the application to be made without notice` kind `the case is one of urgency`
    WHEN JUST permitted THEN
        BRANCH
            IF NOT permitted THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the case is one of urgency or an application under section 37 or 46"
            IF `an action is pending` AND way EQUALS `o 34 r 2 by summons without notice` THEN JUST TRUE
            IF (NOT `an action is pending`) AND way EQUALS `o 34 r 2 by originating application without notice` THEN JUST TRUE
            OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by summons without notice or by originating application without notice (as the case may be)" names the way for each case and is silent on the other combinations
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): see `o 34 r 3(3) this paragraph permits the application to be made without notice`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 4 -- preliminary question of law (section 45)`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- The two bases on which the 14 days run, paragraph (1)(a) and (b).
DECLARE `o 34 r 4(1) basis of the application` IS ONE OF
    `o 34 r 4(1)(a) the agreement of all the parties to the arbitral proceedings`
    `o 34 r 4(1)(b) the permission of the arbitral tribunal`

-- src:5093 | 4. —(1) An application under section 45 to determine any question of law arising in the course of the arbitral proceedings must be made by originating application and served, within 14 days after — ( a )
@ref O 34 r 4(1) the period (src:5093-5093)
`o 34 r 4(1) the period for making and serving the application` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- src:5093 | 4. —(1) An application under section 45 to determine any question of law arising in the course of the arbitral proceedings must be made by originating application and served, within 14 days after — ( a )
-- src:5094 | the agreement of all the parties to the arbitral proceedings; or
-- src:5095 | ( b )
-- src:5096 | the permission of the arbitral tribunal has been obtained.
@ref O 34 r 4(1) (src:5093-5096)
GIVEN kind IS A `o 34 r 2 kind of application`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 34 r 4(1) the application must be made by originating application and served` MEANS
    IF kind EQUALS `o 34 r 2(1)(d) application to determine a question of law under section 45`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An application under section 45 to determine any question of law arising in the course of the arbitral proceedings"

-- The date after which the 14 days run: the date of the agreement, or the date the permission was obtained.
-- The count from that date is O 3 r 3.
-- src:5093 | 4. —(1) An application under section 45 to determine any question of law arising in the course of the arbitral proceedings must be made by originating application and served, within 14 days after — ( a )
-- src:5094 | the agreement of all the parties to the arbitral proceedings; or
-- src:5095 | ( b )
-- src:5096 | the permission of the arbitral tribunal has been obtained.
@ref O 34 r 4(1) (src:5093-5096)
GIVEN kind IS A `o 34 r 2 kind of application`
      basis IS A `o 34 r 4(1) basis of the application`
      `the date of the agreement of all the parties` IS A DATE
      `the date the permission of the arbitral tribunal was obtained` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`o 34 r 4(1) the date after which the period runs` MEANS
    IF kind EQUALS `o 34 r 2(1)(d) application to determine a question of law under section 45`
    THEN CONSIDER basis
        WHEN `o 34 r 4(1)(a) the agreement of all the parties to the arbitral proceedings` THEN JUST `the date of the agreement of all the parties`
        WHEN `o 34 r 4(1)(b) the permission of the arbitral tribunal` THEN JUST `the date the permission of the arbitral tribunal was obtained`
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An application under section 45"

-- The same question as a yes/no: does paragraph (1)'s period run for this application at all?
-- src:5093 | 4. —(1) An application under section 45 to determine any question of law arising in the course of the arbitral proceedings must be made by originating application and served, within 14 days after — ( a )
-- src:5094 | the agreement of all the parties to the arbitral proceedings; or
-- src:5095 | ( b )
-- src:5096 | the permission of the arbitral tribunal has been obtained.
@ref O 34 r 4(1) (src:5093-5096)
GIVEN kind IS A `o 34 r 2 kind of application`
      `the date the application was made` IS A DATE
      `the date the application was served` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 34 r 4(1) the application is made and served in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (kind EQUALS `o 34 r 2(1)(d) application to determine a question of law under section 45`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "An application under section 45"
        IF `the date the application was made` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` AND `the date the application was served` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be made by originating application and served, within 14 days after"

-- src:5097 | (2) For the purpose of paragraph (1), the agreement or permission must be made or given in writing.
@ref O 34 r 4(2) (src:5097-5097)
