-- src:5098 | (3) Where an application under section 45 is made without the agreement in writing of all the other parties to the arbitral proceedings but with the permission of the arbitral tribunal, the affidavits filed by the parties must set out any evidence relied on by the parties in support of their contention that the Court should, or should not, allow the application.
@ref O 34 r 4(3) (src:5098-5098)
GIVEN kind IS A `o 34 r 2 kind of application`
      `the application is made without the agreement in writing of all the other parties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made with the permission of the arbitral tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 34 r 4(3) the duty arises that the affidavits set out the evidence relied on` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (kind EQUALS `o 34 r 2(1)(d) application to determine a question of law under section 45`) THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an application under section 45"
        IF `the application is made without the agreement in writing of all the other parties` AND `the application is made with the permission of the arbitral tribunal` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an application under section 45 is made without the agreement in writing of all the other parties but with the permission of the arbitral tribunal"

-- src:5098 | (3) Where an application under section 45 is made without the agreement in writing of all the other parties to the arbitral proceedings but with the permission of the arbitral tribunal, the affidavits filed by the parties must set out any evidence relied on by the parties in support of their contention that the Court should, or should not, allow the application.
@ref O 34 r 4(3) (src:5098-5098)
GIVEN kind IS A `o 34 r 2 kind of application`
      `the application is made without the agreement in writing of all the other parties` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is made with the permission of the arbitral tribunal` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the affidavits set out any evidence relied on in support of the contention that the Court should, or should not, allow the application` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 34 r 4(3) the affidavits set out the evidence relied on` MEANS
    CONSIDER `o 34 r 4(3) the duty arises that the affidavits set out the evidence relied on` kind `the application is made without the agreement in writing of all the other parties` `the application is made with the permission of the arbitral tribunal`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the affidavits set out any evidence relied on in support of the contention that the Court should, or should not, allow the application`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must set out"; the text does not say what follows (O 3 r 2(4), outside this range, lists what the Court may do)
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the duty does not arise; see the companion `o 34 r 4(3) the duty arises that the affidavits set out the evidence relied on`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the application is not one under section 45

