    `o 34 r 14(2)(b) sending a copy to the debtor at the debtor's usual or last known place of residence or business`
    `o 34 r 14(2)(c) such other manner as the Court may direct`
    `o 34 r 14(2) some other manner`

-- src:5200 | (2) An order granting permission must be drawn up by or on behalf of the creditor and must be served on the debtor — ( a )
-- src:5201 | by delivering a copy to the debtor personally;
-- src:5202 | ( b )
-- src:5203 | by sending a copy to the debtor at the debtor’s usual or last known place of residence or business; or
-- src:5204 | ( c )
-- src:5205 | in such other manner as the Court may direct.
@ref O 34 r 14(2) (src:5200-5205)
GIVEN `the order is drawn up by or on behalf of the creditor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 34 r 14(2) the order granting permission is drawn up as the paragraph requires` MEANS
    IF `the order is drawn up by or on behalf of the creditor`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must be drawn up by or on behalf of the creditor"; the text does not say what follows (O 3 r 2(4), outside this range, lists what the Court may do)

-- src:5200 | (2) An order granting permission must be drawn up by or on behalf of the creditor and must be served on the debtor — ( a )
-- src:5201 | by delivering a copy to the debtor personally;
-- src:5202 | ( b )
-- src:5203 | by sending a copy to the debtor at the debtor’s usual or last known place of residence or business; or
-- src:5204 | ( c )
-- src:5205 | in such other manner as the Court may direct.
@ref O 34 r 14(2) (src:5200-5205)
GIVEN manner IS A `o 34 r 14(2) manner of serving the order`
      `the Court directed that manner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 34 r 14(2) the order is served on the debtor in a manner the paragraph names` MEANS
    CONSIDER manner
    WHEN `o 34 r 14(2)(a) delivering a copy to the debtor personally` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 34 r 14(2)(b) sending a copy to the debtor at the debtor's usual or last known place of residence or business` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `o 34 r 14(2)(c) such other manner as the Court may direct` THEN
        IF `the Court directed that manner`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must be served ... in such other manner as the Court may direct"; the Court gave no direction (O 3 r 2(4), outside this range, lists what the Court may do)
    WHEN `o 34 r 14(2) some other manner` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must be served ... (a) ... (b) ... or (c)"; the text does not say what follows service in another manner

