-- Paragraph (4).  The period is 14 days after service of the order, or, for service out of Singapore, "such other
-- period as the Court may fix".  The debtor "may apply to set aside the order" within it, and "the award must not be
-- enforced until after the expiration of that period or, if the debtor applies within that period to set aside the
-- order, until after the application is finally disposed of".
-- src:5207 | (4) Within 14 days after service of the order or, if the order is to be served out of Singapore, within such other period as the Court may fix, the debtor may apply to set aside the order and the award must not be enforced until after the expiration of that period or, if the debtor applies within that period to set aside the order, until after the application is finally disposed of.
@ref O 34 r 14(4) the period (src:5207-5207)
`o 34 r 14(4) the period for the debtor to apply to set aside the order` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 14
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- src:5207 | (4) Within 14 days after service of the order or, if the order is to be served out of Singapore, within such other period as the Court may fix, the debtor may apply to set aside the order and the award must not be enforced until after the expiration of that period or, if the debtor applies within that period to set aside the order, until after the application is finally disposed of.
@ref O 34 r 14(4) (src:5207-5207)
GIVEN `the order is to be served out of Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the debtor applied to set aside the order` IS A DATE
      `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` IS A DATE
      `the last day of such other period as the Court has fixed` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 34 r 14(4) the debtor's application to set aside the order is made in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the order is to be served out of Singapore`) AND `the date the debtor applied to set aside the order` AT MOST `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF NOT `the order is to be served out of Singapore` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Within 14 days after service of the order"
        OTHERWISE
            CONSIDER `the last day of such other period as the Court has fixed`
            WHEN JUST fixed THEN
                IF `the date the debtor applied to set aside the order` AT MOST fixed
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if the order is to be served out of Singapore, within such other period as the Court may fix"
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the period for service out of Singapore is "such other period as the Court may fix" and the Court has fixed none

-- The bar: "the award must not be enforced until after the expiration of that period or, if the debtor applies within
-- that period to set aside the order, until after the application is finally disposed of" (ruling of 2026-11-05 (d)).
-- TRUE while the award cannot yet be enforced; FALSE once the period has expired with no application, or the
-- application has been finally disposed of.  It never says that the award has been enforced.
-- src:5207 | (4) Within 14 days after service of the order or, if the order is to be served out of Singapore, within such other period as the Court may fix, the debtor may apply to set aside the order and the award must not be enforced until after the expiration of that period or, if the debtor applies within that period to set aside the order, until after the application is finally disposed of.
@ref O 34 r 14(4) (src:5207-5207)
GIVEN `the date asked about` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period` IS A DATE
      `the debtor applied within that period to set aside the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is finally disposed of` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 34 r 14(4) the award cannot yet be enforced` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the date asked about` AT MOST `the last day of the period` THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `the debtor applied within that period to set aside the order` AND NOT `the application is finally disposed of` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the award must not be enforced until after the expiration of that period or, if the debtor applies within that period to set aside the order, until after the application is finally disposed of"

-- The positive twin: the text lifts the bar and grants nothing, so after the bar the answer is NOTHING.
-- src:5207 | (4) Within 14 days after service of the order or, if the order is to be served out of Singapore, within such other period as the Court may fix, the debtor may apply to set aside the order and the award must not be enforced until after the expiration of that period or, if the debtor applies within that period to set aside the order, until after the application is finally disposed of.
@ref O 34 r 14(4) (src:5207-5207)
GIVEN `the date asked about` IS A DATE
      `the last day of the period` IS A DATE
      `the debtor applied within that period to set aside the order` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the application is finally disposed of` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 34 r 14(4) the award may be enforced` MEANS
    CONSIDER `o 34 r 14(4) the award cannot yet be enforced` `the date asked about` `the last day of the period` `the debtor applied within that period to set aside the order` `the application is finally disposed of`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the award must not be enforced until after the expiration of that period"
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is over; the paragraph says only that the award is not to be enforced until then, and grants no right to enforce

-- src:5208 | (5) The copy of the order served on the debtor must state the effect of paragraph (4).
@ref O 34 r 14(5) (src:5208-5208)
GIVEN `the copy of the order served on the debtor states the effect of paragraph (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 34 r 14(5) the copy of the order served states the effect of paragraph (4)` MEANS
    IF `the copy of the order served on the debtor states the effect of paragraph (4)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): a bare "must state the effect of paragraph (4)"; the text does not say what follows (O 3 r 2(4), outside this range, lists what the Court may do)

-- Paragraph (6): a rule of reading, over a small typed representation of what it operates on.
DECLARE `o 34 r 14(6) address that this Rule refers to` IS ONE OF
    `o 34 r 14(6) the usual or last known place of residence or business`
    `o 34 r 14(6) the registered or principal address of the body corporate`

