    IF `the person is a body corporate`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "In relation to a body corporate"

-- src:5209 | (6) In relation to a body corporate, this Rule has effect as if for any reference to the place of residence or business of the creditor or the debtor there were substituted a reference to the registered or principal address of the body corporate.
@ref O 34 r 14(6) (src:5209-5209)
GIVEN `the person is a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `o 34 r 14(6) address that this Rule refers to`
`o 34 r 14(6) the address this Rule refers to for the creditor or the debtor` MEANS
