    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "any written law which provides for the manner in which a document may be served on a body corporate"

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 34 -- the same duties as regulative rules`
-- ===========================================================================

-- Each rule below is the regulative form of a decision function above: a named party, a MUST, MAY or SHANT, the
-- period (in days, counted from the event the paragraph names, at 0) and, where the text gives one, the
-- consequence.  The text names no consequence of a late act in these paragraphs, so a late act is a BREACH of
-- the duty only in the sense that the period has run (O 3 r 2(4), outside this range, lists what the Court may do).
-- The count of days here is a plain count; the count the Rules require is O 3 r 3 (see the decision functions).

DECLARE `o 34 r 4(1) party under Order 34` IS ONE OF
    `o 34 r 4(1) the applicant for a ruling on a question of law`
    `o 34 r 5(3) the defendant`
    `o 34 r 6(3) the appellant`
    `o 34 r 6(5) the respondent`
    `o 34 r 7(3) the claimant`
    `o 34 r 14(4) the debtor`
    `o 34 r 14(4) the creditor`

DECLARE `o 34 r 4(1) act under Order 34` IS ONE OF
    `o 34 r 4(1) make the application and serve it`
    `o 34 r 5(3) file the affidavit opposing the application`
    `o 34 r 6(3) serve the appellant's Case and the core bundle`
    `o 34 r 6(5) file and serve the respondent's Case`
    `o 34 r 7(3) serve the affidavit in support`
    `o 34 r 7(6) file and serve the affidavit opposing permission`
    `o 34 r 7(7)(b) serve the appellant's Case and the core bundle after permission`
    `o 34 r 7(7)(d) file and serve the respondent's Case after permission`
    `o 34 r 7(7)(i) deposit the security after permission`
    `o 34 r 8 apply to the appellate court for permission to appeal`
    `o 34 r 14(4) apply to set aside the order`
    `o 34 r 14(4) enforce the award`

-- src:5093 | 4. —(1) An application under section 45 to determine any question of law arising in the course of the arbitral proceedings must be made by originating application and served, within 14 days after — ( a )
-- src:5094 | the agreement of all the parties to the arbitral proceedings; or
-- src:5095 | ( b )
-- src:5096 | the permission of the arbitral tribunal has been obtained.
@ref O 34 r 4(1) (src:5093-5096)
`o 34 r 4(1) the duty to make and serve the application` MEANS
    PARTY `o 34 r 4(1) the applicant for a ruling on a question of law`
    MUST `o 34 r 4(1) make the application and serve it`
    WITHIN (`o 34 r 4(1) the period for making and serving the application`'s `period length`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 34 r 4(1) the applicant for a ruling on a question of law` BECAUSE "the application was not made and served within 14 days"

-- src:5106 | (3) Within 14 days after being served with the originating application, the defendant, if the defendant wishes to oppose the application, must file an affidavit stating the grounds on which the defendant opposes the application.
@ref O 34 r 5(3) (src:5106-5106)
GIVEN `the defendant wishes to oppose the application` IS A BOOLEAN
`o 34 r 5(3) the duty to file the affidavit opposing the application` MEANS
    IF `the defendant wishes to oppose the application`
    THEN PARTY `o 34 r 5(3) the defendant`
         MUST `o 34 r 5(3) file the affidavit opposing the application`
         WITHIN (`o 34 r 5(3) the period for the defendant's affidavit`'s `period length`)
         HENCE FULFILLED
         LEST BREACH BY `o 34 r 5(3) the defendant` BECAUSE "the affidavit was not filed within 14 days after service of the originating application"
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:5115 | (3) Within 28 days after the originating application is filed, the appellant must serve on the respondent — ( a )
-- src:5116 | the appellant’s Case in the form as provided in paragraph (4); and
-- src:5117 | ( b )
-- src:5118 | a core bundle of documents in the form as provided in paragraph (8).
@ref O 34 r 6(3) (src:5115-5118)
`o 34 r 6(3) the duty to serve the appellant's Case and the core bundle` MEANS
    PARTY `o 34 r 6(3) the appellant`
    MUST `o 34 r 6(3) serve the appellant's Case and the core bundle`
    WITHIN (`o 34 r 6(3) the period for serving the appellant's Case and the core bundle`'s `period length`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 34 r 6(3) the appellant` BECAUSE "the Case and the core bundle were not served within 28 days after the originating application was filed"

-- src:5123 | (5) Within 28 days after being served with the appellant’s Case and the core bundle of documents, the respondent must file and serve a respondent’s Case, which must contain a statement in numbered paragraphs of the grounds on which the respondent contends that the relevant part or parts of the award should be upheld.
@ref O 34 r 6(5) (src:5123-5123)
`o 34 r 6(5) the duty to file and serve the respondent's Case` MEANS
    PARTY `o 34 r 6(5) the respondent`
    MUST `o 34 r 6(5) file and serve the respondent's Case`
    WITHIN (`o 34 r 6(5) the period for the respondent's Case`'s `period length`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 34 r 6(5) the respondent` BECAUSE "the respondent's Case was not filed and served within 28 days after service of the appellant's Case and the core bundle"

-- src:5137 | (3) Within 28 days after the originating application is filed, the claimant must serve on the defendant the affidavit in support of the application for permission as provided in paragraph (4).
@ref O 34 r 7(3) (src:5137-5137)
`o 34 r 7(3) the duty to serve the affidavit in support` MEANS
    PARTY `o 34 r 7(3) the claimant`
    MUST `o 34 r 7(3) serve the affidavit in support`
    WITHIN (`o 34 r 7(3) the period for serving the affidavit in support`'s `period length`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 34 r 7(3) the claimant` BECAUSE "the affidavit in support was not served within 28 days after the originating application was filed"

-- src:5140 | (6) Within 28 days after being served with the originating application and the affidavit in support of the application, the defendant, if the defendant wishes to contest the application for permission, must file and serve an affidavit stating the grounds on which the defendant opposes the grant of permission and setting out any evidence relied on by the defendant relating to the matters mentioned in section 49(5).
@ref O 34 r 7(6) (src:5140-5140)
