    PARTY `o 34 r 6(5) the respondent`
    MUST `o 34 r 7(7)(d) file and serve the respondent's Case after permission`
    WITHIN (`o 34 r 7(7)(d) the period for the respondent's Case`'s `period length`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 34 r 6(5) the respondent` BECAUSE "the respondent's Case was not filed and served within 28 days after service of the appellant's Case and the core bundle"

-- src:5168 | ( i )
-- src:5169 | the appellant must, within 14 days after the Court grants permission to appeal, deposit a sum of $5,000, by way of security for the respondent’s costs of the appeal, in the Registry or with the Accountant ‑ General and obtain a certificate in Form 36;
@ref O 34 r 7(7)(i) (src:5168-5169)
`o 34 r 7(7)(i) the duty to deposit the security after permission` MEANS
    PARTY `o 34 r 6(3) the appellant`
    MUST `o 34 r 7(7)(i) deposit the security after permission`
    WITHIN (`o 34 r 7(7)(i) the period for depositing the security`'s `period length`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 34 r 6(3) the appellant` BECAUSE "the security was not deposited within 14 days after the Court granted permission to appeal"

-- src:5173 | 8. An application under the Act for permission to appeal against a decision of the Court to the appellate court must be made to the appellate court within 14 days after the decision of the Court.
@ref O 34 r 8 (src:5173-5173)
`o 34 r 8 the duty to apply to the appellate court for permission` MEANS
    PARTY `o 34 r 4(1) the applicant for a ruling on a question of law`
    MUST `o 34 r 8 apply to the appellate court for permission to appeal`
    WITHIN (`o 34 r 8 the period for applying to the appellate court for permission`'s `period length`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 34 r 4(1) the applicant for a ruling on a question of law` BECAUSE "the application was not made to the appellate court within 14 days after the decision of the Court"

-- The debtor's permission: a MAY.  On this build a MAY that lapses unused is FULFILLED, so no trace can show the
-- window closing (NOTES.md, what the main binary does not accept); the decision function above does.
-- src:5207 | (4) Within 14 days after service of the order or, if the order is to be served out of Singapore, within such other period as the Court may fix, the debtor may apply to set aside the order and the award must not be enforced until after the expiration of that period or, if the debtor applies within that period to set aside the order, until after the application is finally disposed of.
@ref O 34 r 14(4) (src:5207-5207)
`o 34 r 14(4) the debtor's permission to apply to set aside the order` MEANS
    PARTY `o 34 r 14(4) the debtor`
    MAY `o 34 r 14(4) apply to set aside the order`
    WITHIN (`o 34 r 14(4) the period for the debtor to apply to set aside the order`'s `period length`)
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- The bar on enforcing the award: a SHANT, which is how the deontic mechanism reads an "until": enforcing inside
-- the period is the violation, and the period passing quietly is the prohibition kept.
-- src:5207 | (4) Within 14 days after service of the order or, if the order is to be served out of Singapore, within such other period as the Court may fix, the debtor may apply to set aside the order and the award must not be enforced until after the expiration of that period or, if the debtor applies within that period to set aside the order, until after the application is finally disposed of.
@ref O 34 r 14(4) (src:5207-5207)
`o 34 r 14(4) the bar on enforcing the award` MEANS
    PARTY `o 34 r 14(4) the creditor`
    SHANT `o 34 r 14(4) enforce the award`
    WITHIN (`o 34 r 14(4) the period for the debtor to apply to set aside the order`'s `period length`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `o 34 r 14(4) the creditor` BECAUSE "the award was enforced before the expiration of the period for the debtor to apply to set aside the order"
